// Into a salt hall by its west mouth. Known layout blockers (sites.rs; see REFINE-movement.md): the hall's
// own wall closes off the end of each mouth and four quartz columns stand floor to roof, so the hall is five
// sealed strips and the chest can't be reached without digging; the east mouth's lintel and the limestone
// over it sag in the first seconds and bury a mole standing there (100 to 27 hp in 2 s), so this walk uses
// the west mouth.
